  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B022",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and development of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B003",
    "B007"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. Optical lattice clocks remain the strongest bounded achievement: the magic-wavelength concept solved a central obstacle to precision spectroscopy with many trapped atoms, and its experimental realization became an internationally reproducible regime of exceptional agreement. Katori and Ye retain the most coherent two-person allocation for the defining concept and foundational development. The achievement is mature basic physics because it makes time, gravity, and frequency tests directly measurable with unprecedented control, rather than merely improving a practical clock.",
    "case_against": "The citation must not be allowed to encompass the whole optical-clock enterprise or every later engineering advance. The record still needs to establish precisely which developments are essential to the recognized lattice-clock achievement and how the proposed two-person attribution relates to other enabling contributors. Its strongest case is the established transformation of precision measurement, not a claim that every anticipated fundamental application has already produced a decisive discovery.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson argues that cosmic inflation has exceptional foundational scope and decades of observational constraint, but acknowledges that no distinctive observation uniquely selects inflation over all viable alternatives.",
        "response": "I continue to regard B033 as profound, but that acknowledged empirical limitation matters when comparing it with B022. The lattice-clock result is a sharply specified physical regime whose defining performance can be repeatedly tested across laboratories. Its merit does not depend on support for future applications: the demonstrated capability itself has opened controlled access to relativistic gravity and fundamental-frequency observables."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig favors the mature, foundational conformal field theory of two-dimensional critical phenomena, while recognizing that its connection to directly measurable systems is less immediate than for an instrumental advance.",
        "response": "B027 is an unusually elegant and durable theoretical achievement, and its compact attribution is a real strength. I nevertheless retain B022 because its physical principle and experimental consequences form an equally bounded achievement with exceptionally direct reproducibility. The lattice-clock platform has not only supplied a useful technique; it has made a new domain of precision physical comparison experimentally reliable."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "olsson-eva",
        "point": "Olsson stresses that spherical-aberration correction transformed transmission electron microscopy into an atom-resolving quantitative instrument, but that the respective roles of theory, corrector engineering, implementation, and later development require documentary reconstruction.",
        "response": "I agree that B061 is a major transformation in experimental physics. The unresolved allocation is nevertheless central to its final form: the proposed trio spans a long chain whose essential boundary remains to be reconstructed. B022 has a more compact concept-to-realization structure, provided that we retain the same discipline in separating lattice clocks from the wider optical-clock field."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "The documentary record should determine the exact boundary between Katori's magic-wavelength lattice-clock concept, Ye's defining experimental advances, and other enabling work in the broader optical-clock community.",
      "The final citation should remain confined to the demonstrated optical-lattice-clock achievement and avoid presenting developing applications as completed discoveries."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "Updated review finds no conflict requiring recusal. My long-standing collaborations in attosecond physics concern no shortlisted achievement or credited candidate."
  }
}
